# Release notes for Guardian IDM
This release note provides information about the update in the Guardian IDM.
## May 13, 2026
In this update the expiry of access_token has been increased from 1800 seconds (30 mins) to 7200 seconds (2 hours). This means authenticated sessions now remain valid for a longer duration before requiring renewal.

## Why it matters
- Reduces the frequency of token refresh calls, improving efficiency for applications that make frequent API requests.

- Enhances user experience by minimizing interruptions due to token expiration.

- Lowers authentication overhead, which can improve performance in high-volume integrations.

## Who is impacted
- Developers/integrators using Guardian IDM APIs for authentication and secure access.

- System administrators managing session lifecycles and monitoring token usage.

- End users indirectly benefit from fewer login prompts or session interruptions.

## Setup or compatibility considerations
No changes are required for existing API calls.

## Reference to deeper documentation
For detailed authentication workflows and updated token management guidelines, please refer to the [Guardian IDM API documentation:](https://github.com/Saishis/Alert-Enterprise-Guardian-IDM-External-Services.git)